  "slug": "catching-thief-with-wisdom",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/3649_catching-thief-with-wisdom.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "One evening, a farmer saw someone carrying a large bundle toward the neighboring village. The next day, he discovered that his cotton had been stolen, so he went to ask his clever younger brother, Mike, what to do.",
    "Mike thought for a moment, then invited everyone from the neighboring village to a dance. At the dance, he said, “I’m sorry to bring this up, but my brother’s cotton was stolen yesterday, and the thief has come here today. Look—even now, there’s still cotton stuck to his face and hair!”",
    "At that, one man who had no cotton on his face or hair nervously touched them again and again. Mike walked up to him and said, “He’s the thief!” And that was how the cotton thief was caught."
  ],
  "english_full": "One evening, a farmer saw someone carrying a large bundle toward the neighboring village. The next day, he discovered that his cotton had been stolen, so he went to ask his clever younger brother, Mike, what to do.\n\nMike thought for a moment, then invited everyone from the neighboring village to a dance. At the dance, he said, “I’m sorry to bring this up, but my brother’s cotton was stolen yesterday, and the thief has come here today. Look—even now, there’s still cotton stuck to his face and hair!”\n\nAt that, one man who had no cotton on his face or hair nervously touched them again and again. Mike walked up to him and said, “He’s the thief!” And that was how the cotton thief was caught.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "О́дним ве́чером дехка́нин у́видел, как кто́-то не́с крупный па́чку в направле́нии к сосе́дней дере́вне. На сле́дующий день он обнару́жил, что его́ хло́пок был укра́ден, поэ́тому он пошёл спра́шивать своего́ ло́вкого мла́дшего бра́та Ма́ртина, что́ делать.",
    "Ма́ртин ду́мал не́который моме́нт, а затем пригласи́л всех из сосе́дней дере́вни на та́нец. На та́нце он ска́зал: “Мне жаль поднима́ть эту́ тему, но вчера́ у́ моего бра́та укра́ли хло́пок, а вор пришёл сего́дня сюда́. Смотрите — даже те́перь на его́ лице́ и во́лосах оста́ётся хло́пок!”",
    "Услы́шав это, о́дин человек, у ко́торого не́ было хло́пка на лице́ или во́лосах, не́рвно трогал их па́ки и па́ки. Ма́ртин подо́шёл к нему и ска́зал: “Он — вор!” И так вор-хло́пка был пойма́н."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Ódnim vécherom deýkhanin uvídél, kak któ-to néss krúpnyy páchku v napravléníyi k sosédney derévnye. Na sléduyushchiy dyén' on obnarúzhíl, chto yegó klópok byl ukráden, poétomu on poshóly spráshivat' svoyego lóvkogo mládshego bráta Mártina, chtó delát'.",
    "Mártin dúmal nékotorýy momént, a zatem prigláshíl vsekh iz sosédney derévnye na tánets. Na tánce on skázal: “Mne zhal' podnimát' etú téma, no vchéra u móyego bráta ukráli klópok, a vor prishél segódnya syuda. Smotrité — dázhe téper' na yego litse i vôlosakh ostáyetsya klópok!”",
    "Uslýshav èto, odín chelovék, u kotorogo né bylo klópka na litse ili vôlosakh, nérvno trógal ikh páki i páki. Mártin podóshël k nemu i skázal: “On — vor!” I tak vor-klópka byl poymán."
  ],
